### The chunked-prefill logits trap

Computing logits for every prompt position at 64K materializes a `vocab × 64K` tensor. For
the Llama 3.2 vocabulary that is
**{{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.0.prefill_logits_bytes_64k.bf16 | iec }} in bf16** and
**{{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.0.prefill_logits_bytes_64k.fp32 | iec }} in fp32**
(logits are commonly upcast), larger than the GPU's entire VRAM. Chunked prefill with
last-position-only logits is mandatory, as the brief says.

## Reading the table

- **Llama-3.2-1B is a sensible primary.** Weights take {{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.0.weights_bytes_safetensors | iec }} on disk, and 64K of bf16 KV takes {{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.0.kv_bytes_by_context_bf16.65536 | iec }}. **Its full 64K KV cache fits in free VRAM.** The GPU KV budget in every LazyKV sweep is therefore an *imposed* constraint, not a physical one. That is legitimate, since the budget sweep is the experiment, but the README and paper must say so plainly.
- **Llama-3.2-3B in bf16 does not work as the stress model.** Its weights alone take {{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.1.weights_bytes_safetensors | iec }}, leaving room for at most {{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.1.max_context_bf16_in_free_vram | int }} bf16 KV tokens even before activations. 4-bit weights (NF4, as the brief proposes) are required, which needs `bitsandbytes`: a new dependency that needs sign-off. The NF4 weight size is **not measured**.
- **Qwen2.5-1.5B** has aggressive GQA ({{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.2.gqa_group }}:1), which makes its KV smaller per token than the 1B Llama's ({{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.2.kv_bytes_per_token_bf16 | iec }} vs {{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.0.kv_bytes_per_token_bf16 | iec }}). Its `max_position_embeddings` is {{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.2.max_position_embeddings | int }}, so a 64K run would be outside its native window. It is the least interesting candidate for a KV-pressure study, exactly as §B3 warns.
- **Phi-3-mini (4k)** has no GQA and the largest per-token KV ({{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.3.kv_bytes_per_token_bf16 | iec }}). But its bf16 weights ({{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.3.weights_bytes_safetensors | iec }}) exceed free VRAM, and this variant's `max_position_embeddings` is {{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.3.max_position_embeddings | int }}. It is not usable here without a long-context variant plus 4-bit weights, so it is dropped.
- **SmolLM2-1.7B** has no GQA ({{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.4.kv_bytes_per_token_bf16 | iec }} per token), which makes KV genuinely dominant. Its `max_position_embeddings` of {{ phase0.kv_memory_model.models.4.max_position_embeddings | int }} rules out the 32K headline experiment. It could still serve as a short-context, high-KV-pressure secondary model.

